# Office ONE — example environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust as needed. The app reads `.env` ONLY in
# development (packaged builds ignore it). There are NO required values and NO
# secrets — the app is fully offline and stores everything in a local SQLite
# database. Every value below is optional.
#
# Real environment variables (exported in your shell) always take precedence
# over values in `.env`.

# Override where the SQLite database + backups live. Without it the app uses the
# folder chosen on first launch (saved in %APPDATA%\office-one-location.json).
# An override may point at an empty folder (a fresh database is created there).
# Useful for testing or a portable install. Use an absolute path.
# OFFICEONE_DATA_DIR is also accepted; OFFICE_ONE_DATA_DIR wins if both are set.
# OFFICE_ONE_DATA_DIR=D:\path\to\data

# Dev-only, for testing the first-run folder choice without touching the real
# setting: where the saved-location file (and the setup profile beside it)
# live, and a folder that answers every setup dialog unattended.
# OFFICE_ONE_LOCATION_FILE=D:\path\to\scratch\office-one-location.json
# OFFICE_ONE_TEST_PICK_DIR=D:\path\to\scratch\data
